    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d870">

                <pb facs="0878" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg620"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.115Am319/46</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-30T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 30, 1915, 7 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2516. Department informed by owners of <hi rendition="#italic">Hocking</hi> and
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Genesee</hi> that British Government intends to
                    requisition these vessels.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d870-f1"/> If information
                    correct, enter at once vigorous protest against any such action and insist on
                    prize court proceedings being pushed to determine question of ownership.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d870-f1" n="4" xml:id="d870-f1-content">
                <p>See the order in council of March 23, providing for the requisitioning of “a ship
                    in respect of which no final decree of condemnation has been made,” <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg366">p. 366</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
